        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: соблюдать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "соблюдать (soblyudát) — \"to observe, to keep (a rule)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Все должны соблюдать правила. Vse dolzhný soblyudát právila. Everyone must observe the rules."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective соблюсти, rare. Соблюдать закон, диету, тишину."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "соблюдать (soblyudát) is built from со- and блюсти \"to guard, to keep\", an old Slavic verb also behind наблюдать \"to observe\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
